Day 286/300: Minimum Number of Flips to Make the Binary String Alternating

Problem Statement #1888

Problem Statement Explanation:

Given a binary string s, you can perform two types of operations:
Type 1: Remove the first character of the string and append it to the end.
Type 2: Choose any character in the string and flip it (0→1 or 1→0).
Return the minimum number of Type 2 operations (flips) needed to make s alternating after any number of Type 1 operations.
An alternating string is a string where no two adjacent characters are equal (e.g., "0101" or "1010").

Solution Approach:

The core challenge is the Type 1 operation. 
Instead of physically rotating the string, we can simulate all possible rotations by doubling the string: s + s. 
Any substring of length n within this doubled string represents a valid state achievable via Type 1 operations.

Key Logic
Target Patterns: There are only two possible alternating strings for any given length: one starting with 0 and one starting with 1.
Sliding Window: We maintain a window of size n and slide it across the doubled string.
Difference Tracking: We count how many characters in the current window differ from the two target patterns.
Update Min: As we slide the window (adding one character on the right and removing one from the left), we update the total differences and track the global minimum.

Here's the Code:

class Solution {
    public int minFlips(String s) {
        int n = s.length();
        int diff1 = 0, diff2 = 0;
        int minFlips = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        
        for (int i = 0; i < 2 * n; i++) {
            char c = s.charAt(i % n);
            
            if (c != (i % 2 == 0 ? '0' : '1')) diff1++;
            if (c != (i % 2 == 0 ? '1' : '0')) diff2++;
            
            if (i >= n) {
                if (s.charAt((i - n) % n) != ((i - n) % 2 == 0 ? '0' : '1')) diff1--;
                if (s.charAt((i - n) % n) != ((i - n) % 2 == 0 ? '1' : '0')) diff2--;
            }
            
            if (i >= n - 1) {
                minFlips = Math.min(minFlips, Math.min(diff1, diff2));
            }
        }
        
        return minFlips;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity:	O(1)



